## Acceptance Criteria

### AC-1: Access Control

- [ ] Each role sees only the data permitted by policy rules
- [ ] Masked fields show masked values for non-exempt roles
- [ ] Unmasked access is restricted to documented exempt roles

### AC-2: Policy Enforcement

- [ ] Policies are applied to all documented target objects
- [ ] New tables matching governed patterns are flagged for policy attachment
- [ ] Policy changes require approval (change control applies)

### AC-3: Audit Trail

- [ ] Policy creation/modification is logged in ACCESS_HISTORY
- [ ] Role grants are traceable to approver
- [ ] Compliance report can enumerate all governed objects and their policies

### AC-4: Operational Safety

- [ ] Policies fail-closed (deny access on error, not allow)
- [ ] Removing a policy requires explicit confirmation (not silent)
- [ ] Testing policy changes in non-production before applying to production

---

## Edge Cases

| Scenario | Expected Behavior |
|----------|-------------------|
| User has multiple roles | Most permissive policy applies (Snowflake default) |
| New column added to governed table | Column is unmasked until policy is updated — flag in drift detection |
| Policy function errors at runtime | Query fails (fail-closed); alert ops team |
| Role dropped while policy references it | Policy continues to function; clean up stale references |
| Cross-database query | Policies follow the data (applied at column level, not query level) |

